WEBVTT

00:14.020 --> 00:18.050
You figured out how to use the Black Box?

00:18.050 --> 00:18.480
Yeah.

00:19.450 --> 00:24.310
While I was carrying it around,
it just came to me.

00:24.310 --> 00:28.490
But I don't think I can make
it work without your help.

00:28.490 --> 00:29.120
My help?

00:29.580 --> 00:33.880
So it's the type of artifact that
requires the power of an Alchemist?

00:33.880 --> 00:35.880
Okay, what do I need to do?

00:35.880 --> 00:38.600
Um... Think of me.

00:38.600 --> 00:39.380
Think of you?

00:39.820 --> 00:43.300
Yeah. This little one knows me now,

00:43.300 --> 00:46.260
so tell it about the me that you know.

00:48.250 --> 00:50.680
The Marina I know...

01:04.840 --> 01:06.380
I was right!

01:06.380 --> 01:08.440
It looks like a samurai sword,

01:08.440 --> 01:10.700
and a bit like your bastard sword, too.

01:10.700 --> 01:12.330
How does that work?

01:13.920 --> 01:14.830
It's a secret!

01:15.110 --> 01:16.510
G-Give me a hint!

01:16.510 --> 01:22.800
Well, let's just say... a baby needs
not just a mom, but a dad, too.

01:22.800 --> 01:24.960
I have no idea what that means!

01:26.310 --> 01:28.970
Aren't you excited to see what the
future holds for this little one,

01:28.970 --> 01:30.340
Papa?

01:40.110 --> 01:47.070
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

03:02.020 --> 03:03.130
(Episode 7: The Pale, Immortal Ruler)

03:03.130 --> 03:05.080
(Episode 7: The Pale, Immortal Ruler)
Take care in there.

03:05.080 --> 03:08.030
Don't feel the need to achieve
more than you did the first time.

03:08.470 --> 03:11.060
You've already accomplished
more than enough.

03:11.060 --> 03:12.440
I know.

03:12.440 --> 03:16.030
If I feel like we're in danger, I'll use
the Scroll of Exit to bail right away.

03:16.500 --> 03:17.710
Begin livestream.

03:17.710 --> 03:19.040
Beginning livestream.

03:20.400 --> 03:21.670
Clover here.

03:21.670 --> 03:24.790
It's been three days since our first
assault on Achromatic Darkness.

03:25.360 --> 03:27.660
We're about to launch our second assault.

03:28.310 --> 03:33.930
Our goal this time is to reach the stairway
area of the third floor and look for oddities.

03:34.360 --> 03:38.870
Upon finding any, we'll make judgment
calls as needed and retreat if necessary.

03:38.870 --> 03:40.830
Let's have fun, but be careful.

03:40.830 --> 03:42.310
- Right!
- Got it!

03:43.300 --> 03:45.160
It's gone smoothly so far.

03:45.160 --> 03:50.320
Yes, the layout of the dungeon hasn't
changed since our first assault.

03:50.770 --> 03:52.820
The question is what lies ahead.

03:53.190 --> 03:55.820
I can see the second floor coming up.

03:56.210 --> 03:59.670
So what will we be up against?
A demon or a snake?

04:00.430 --> 04:02.080
Let's all stay alert.

04:03.850 --> 04:06.580
Well, this is... something...

04:07.720 --> 04:09.160
It's seriously crazy.

04:09.160 --> 04:10.710
We're inside a dungeon, but...

04:10.710 --> 04:12.090
...it has a sky!

04:13.870 --> 04:15.090
Let's just calm down.

04:15.810 --> 04:18.900
There were records of floors that
took the form of outdoor areas.

04:18.900 --> 04:22.410
But Yuke, this is still
just the second floor.

04:22.410 --> 04:25.850
Yeah. This showed up too early.

04:26.350 --> 04:29.560
Floors like this have only
been confirmed to appear

04:29.560 --> 04:32.560
no higher than the twentieth floor down.

04:32.560 --> 04:37.520
So this is what they mean when they
say the dungeon's layout changes...

04:37.520 --> 04:40.620
That's why Achromatic Darkness
is regarded as so unusual.

04:41.010 --> 04:46.140
But is the abnormality the simple fact
that outdoor areas appear so early on

04:46.140 --> 04:49.460
or that deeper floors are
moving up toward the top?

04:50.190 --> 04:52.160
Is Wind Priming working?

04:52.160 --> 04:54.910
No, the wind's too strong.

04:54.910 --> 04:55.880
I thought so.

04:56.540 --> 04:58.890
I'd like to check our
surroundings first, but...

04:59.270 --> 05:01.720
I didn't even think to bring a telescope.

05:01.720 --> 05:05.780
Shall I look around with magic?
I can use Telescope Eye.

05:05.780 --> 05:08.440
Please do. Start on our right.

05:08.440 --> 05:10.150
Okay, then.

05:12.580 --> 05:14.220
Y-You okay?

05:14.220 --> 05:15.400
I'm good.

05:15.860 --> 05:19.740
That which is both far and near,
look through my eyes.

05:19.740 --> 05:21.160
Telescope Eye!

05:23.800 --> 05:25.160
There's nothing.

05:25.450 --> 05:27.590
No signs of any monsters.

05:27.590 --> 05:29.540
Turn left next, please.

05:31.870 --> 05:33.260
Something's there.

05:33.260 --> 05:33.800
Huh?

05:33.800 --> 05:34.830
A house.

05:35.180 --> 05:35.990
A house?

05:35.990 --> 05:39.180
Yeah. A small house with a blue roof.

05:39.180 --> 05:40.800
It's pretty far.

05:41.550 --> 05:44.220
My eyes are worn out...

05:44.220 --> 05:46.310
Okay, got it. Thanks.

05:47.600 --> 05:51.310
Master, is it normal for
houses to be in dungeons?

05:51.560 --> 05:56.110
It's not unusual to find
ruins of buildings in them,

05:56.110 --> 05:58.400
but a whole house...

05:59.060 --> 06:01.830
We should probably assume
something's going on.

06:03.320 --> 06:04.330
Is something wrong?

06:05.270 --> 06:09.830
That sun. I hope it's just an artifact
that serves as an alternate light source.

06:10.250 --> 06:13.270
It's an artifact? I want it.

06:13.270 --> 06:15.840
But if it really is the sun...

06:16.530 --> 06:18.840
When it sets, it'll be nighttime.

06:18.840 --> 06:23.190
Right. That in itself could be
a trap or some kind of gimmick.

06:23.190 --> 06:25.850
We should act while the sun's up.

06:26.410 --> 06:27.740
I see it!

06:33.860 --> 06:35.860
It looks newly built.

06:37.220 --> 06:38.810
I don't sense any mana.

06:38.810 --> 06:40.610
Should we check inside?

06:41.320 --> 06:45.950
It's definitely weird to find an
ordinary house inside a dungeon.

06:45.950 --> 06:48.120
Could it be a safety area?

06:48.640 --> 06:52.880
No, it's not. If this is considered
normal within Achromatic Darkness,

06:52.880 --> 06:55.020
maybe we should assume
it's an abnormality.

06:55.020 --> 06:56.630
My, my!

06:56.630 --> 06:59.630
I haven't had visitors in so long.

06:59.630 --> 07:01.800
Would you like some tea?

07:01.800 --> 07:05.140
If you're hungry, I also have pumpkin pie.

07:05.140 --> 07:06.270
Master!

07:06.270 --> 07:09.560
Yeah. There's no way a person
could be living in a dungeon.

07:09.560 --> 07:12.150
But I don't sense any evil or malice.

07:12.860 --> 07:14.900
Just what is that?

07:15.240 --> 07:17.520
Wait... Who are you?

07:17.520 --> 07:19.900
Why are you living here?

07:19.900 --> 07:24.680
Well... that's a very long story.

07:24.680 --> 07:27.870
We shouldn't talk out here.
Do come inside.

07:28.160 --> 07:32.780
I'm sorry, but we're adventurers,
and this is a dungeon.

07:32.780 --> 07:35.130
We can't accept your offer.

07:35.370 --> 07:37.000
Oh, is that so?

07:37.450 --> 07:39.940
But the sun will be going down soon.

07:43.320 --> 07:44.430
Yuke!

07:45.540 --> 07:46.620
An illusion?!

07:47.300 --> 07:49.180
The house is getting bigger!

07:49.180 --> 07:52.520
Something's off with the spirits!
The balance is falling apart!

07:52.520 --> 07:53.690
Yuke?

07:55.880 --> 07:57.160
What's going on?!

07:58.170 --> 08:01.150
You see? Night is coming.

08:05.190 --> 08:08.640
What a shame. You were just a step away.

08:09.130 --> 08:11.160
I almost crossed the threshold!

08:12.660 --> 08:15.950
So you knew it would be
unwise to come inside.

08:15.950 --> 08:17.790
I don't dislike clever boys.

08:21.160 --> 08:22.050
So that's it!

08:23.550 --> 08:24.750
(The Pale, Immortal Ruler Lady Persephone)

08:24.750 --> 08:26.510
(The Pale, Immortal Ruler Lady Persephone)
Lady Persephone...

08:26.510 --> 08:29.220
(The Pale, Immortal Ruler Lady Persephone)
The goddess who reverses life and death!

08:29.220 --> 08:32.810
(The Pale, Immortal Ruler Lady Persephone)
Oh? So you know my name... Yuke, was it?

08:33.230 --> 08:38.120
I have spent thousands of years trapped in
the tedium of guiding the souls of the dead.

08:38.120 --> 08:40.820
I'm so glad you've found your way here.

08:41.120 --> 08:44.570
Now that you're here,
none of you shall leave alive.

08:44.870 --> 08:49.330
You have no choice but to accept
that your lives will be

08:49.330 --> 08:52.080
used to stave off my
boredom for all eternity!

08:54.790 --> 08:58.330
Great, Pale, Immortal Ruler,
may we meet again...

08:58.670 --> 09:02.090
when my time in this world
comes to an end.

09:09.100 --> 09:11.850
I will not forget you said that.

09:19.000 --> 09:20.480
Back to the stairway!

09:24.070 --> 09:25.360
Physical Enchant!

09:25.990 --> 09:27.990
(Enhanced Stamina, Enhanced Leg
Strength, Enhanced Arm Strength)

09:27.990 --> 09:30.490
That was Lady Persephone.

09:30.490 --> 09:32.800
The Pale, Immortal Ruler?!

09:33.560 --> 09:35.250
So in other words, we're...

09:35.960 --> 09:39.000
...in the land of the dead right now!

09:39.000 --> 09:42.690
It feels like my mana's
being sucked out of me...

09:42.690 --> 09:44.510
Hurry! Before our mana runs dry!

09:45.000 --> 09:46.870
Night monsters will show up soon!

09:49.480 --> 09:50.760
Everyone okay?

09:51.000 --> 09:53.180
I-I'm okay, I think.

09:53.180 --> 09:55.590
I'm fine, too.

09:55.590 --> 09:57.790
Exhausted, but fine.

09:57.790 --> 09:59.440
End livestream.

09:59.440 --> 10:00.770
Goodnight.

10:02.810 --> 10:06.780
I think the nighttime in the land of
death drained our mana and vitality.

10:07.150 --> 10:09.640
I can't even use Refresh Mana right now.

10:09.640 --> 10:11.780
Um, Yuke...

10:14.220 --> 10:15.790
What is this?

10:16.140 --> 10:18.040
Persephone's curse?

10:19.000 --> 10:19.910
Yeah...

10:20.430 --> 10:25.230
I'm sorry. I don't think I
have the power to remove it.

10:25.230 --> 10:29.180
Don't worry about it. I'll hit
up the temple when we get home.

10:31.680 --> 10:35.520
Just what was that place earlier?

10:35.520 --> 10:39.820
I think it was the Grey Field
mentioned in the Remazurka Epic.

10:39.820 --> 10:42.190
So you also knew about that phrase?

10:42.480 --> 10:46.400
"Great, Pale, Immortal Ruler,
may we meet again...

10:46.400 --> 10:49.460
when my time in this world
comes to an end."

10:50.020 --> 10:54.040
The protagonist in the Remazurka Epic
said that, and it kept him alive.

10:54.040 --> 10:55.450
I'm just glad it worked.

10:56.230 --> 10:58.680
This is a realm that is not of this world,

10:58.680 --> 11:01.350
ruled by Lady Persephone,
the Pale, Immortal Ruler.

11:01.350 --> 11:05.210
Here, the peaceful daytime of life and
the nighttime of devastating death

11:05.210 --> 11:07.150
repeat in an endless cycle.

11:07.150 --> 11:09.470
It's a realm where dualities
mingle together—

11:09.890 --> 11:12.050
in other words, where they reverse.

11:12.050 --> 11:13.090
Reverse?

11:13.440 --> 11:17.210
Day and night, life and death,
age and youth...

11:17.210 --> 11:18.600
Everything is reversed.

11:18.600 --> 11:19.480
What?!

11:20.350 --> 11:22.840
It must be a trait unique
to Achromatic Darkness.

11:22.840 --> 11:25.320
Its true nature as a dungeon—

11:25.320 --> 11:29.990
the nature of a dungeon
that houses an Abyss Gate.

11:30.560 --> 11:34.490
I think an Abyss Gate really
is a doorway to another world.

11:34.490 --> 11:38.200
And what does that have to
do with Achromatic Darkness?

11:38.200 --> 11:41.360
I think it's replicating
the world it connects to.

11:41.360 --> 11:43.360
The world it connects to?

11:43.360 --> 11:44.500
A different world.

11:44.810 --> 11:47.080
Achromatic Darkness itself
is another world?

11:47.080 --> 11:49.380
No, a dungeon that copies one.

11:50.190 --> 11:56.580
I believe the Abyss Gate is where the edges
of many worlds, including ours, overlap.

11:57.670 --> 12:02.210
If that's the case, maybe this dungeon
itself is capable of producing

12:02.210 --> 12:05.900
a limited recreation of another world—
of the Grey Field.

12:08.850 --> 12:13.640
So there you have it. At least half of
that is old Saga's guesswork, though.

12:13.640 --> 12:14.660
I see...

12:15.010 --> 12:18.310
But that was still just the
second floor, wasn't it?

12:19.990 --> 12:20.990
This is bad.

12:20.990 --> 12:21.910
What is?

12:21.910 --> 12:25.170
What floor are we on right now?

12:26.300 --> 12:30.940
Wait... Could this be the 30th floor

12:30.940 --> 12:34.340
that the vanguard conquered 20 years ago?

12:34.340 --> 12:35.550
Could it be...

12:35.550 --> 12:38.290
Did we skip a bunch of floors?

12:39.720 --> 12:40.860
It's possible.

12:41.380 --> 12:46.060
Maybe the second floor we saw was not
the second floor in the records.

12:46.060 --> 12:47.900
Oh, that's it!

12:47.900 --> 12:49.670
It's like Rain said!

12:49.670 --> 12:52.570
The stairways are skipping us
ahead to different floors!

12:53.020 --> 12:54.740
How can you be so sure?

12:54.740 --> 12:59.420
Well, no one's seen a dungeon change
its appearance before, right?

12:59.970 --> 13:00.830
You mean...

13:00.830 --> 13:03.330
It's not that the dungeon changes.

13:03.330 --> 13:07.330
We're being skipped to different
floors from the stairways.

13:07.680 --> 13:08.990
Yeah...

13:08.990 --> 13:11.150
That would explain why it looked like

13:11.150 --> 13:14.090
the layout had changed between
coming in and going out.

13:14.090 --> 13:15.590
Oh, I get it!

13:16.140 --> 13:17.070
What should we do?

13:17.800 --> 13:19.470
Get out of here right now?

13:19.470 --> 13:21.930
Master, you're pushing too hard.

13:21.930 --> 13:23.380
Let's rest first.

13:23.380 --> 13:25.690
Considering the time and
our strength levels,

13:25.690 --> 13:27.480
we should stay here longer.

13:27.810 --> 13:30.000
We can think about it
after we've recovered.

13:30.000 --> 13:32.670
And no matter what you decide,
we're with you.

13:32.670 --> 13:35.720
Yep. So let's just rest for now.

13:37.140 --> 13:38.990
Get plenty of rest, okay?

13:39.510 --> 13:41.380
I will. You guys, too.

13:45.600 --> 13:47.140
Hey. Get up.

13:53.790 --> 13:54.910
Simon!

13:56.780 --> 13:59.220
Simon! Why are you here?!

13:59.840 --> 14:02.590
Because I followed you here, obviously.

14:02.590 --> 14:03.690
What are you after?!

14:03.690 --> 14:05.720
Hey, relax.

14:05.720 --> 14:08.020
We have the initiative here.

14:12.800 --> 14:14.110
What did you do to them?!

14:14.110 --> 14:17.560
We only put them to sleep for a bit.

14:17.560 --> 14:21.620
Yo, do you see the thing around
this little runt's neck?

14:22.090 --> 14:22.870
A Slave Collar?! Why do you have that?

14:22.870 --> 14:25.120
(Slave Collar)
A Slave Collar?! Why do you have that?

14:25.120 --> 14:28.360
A kind sponsor of ours gave it to us.

14:28.360 --> 14:31.380
They seemed to have a hell
of a grudge against you.

14:31.640 --> 14:32.810
A grudge?

14:32.810 --> 14:36.560
With this, that girl will
do exactly as I say.

14:36.560 --> 14:39.270
What do you hope to
accomplish by using that?!

14:39.270 --> 14:41.140
If word gets out, you'll be a criminal!

14:41.570 --> 14:45.160
We're doomed either way
if nothing changes.

14:45.160 --> 14:50.140
Imagine being branded as criminals and
exiled because of a little difference in opinion.

14:51.970 --> 14:56.680
So I have a good idea that'll
keep us both out of trouble.

14:56.680 --> 14:59.220
Why don't we patch things up between us?

14:59.220 --> 14:59.900
Huh?!

15:00.160 --> 15:03.910
After all, you're a part of Thunder Pike.

15:05.450 --> 15:07.670
I have the official paperwork here.

15:07.670 --> 15:09.290
Mind signing this?

15:09.720 --> 15:12.080
"Upon the start of the mission,

15:12.080 --> 15:15.290
Clover had requested an
alliance with Thunder Pike."

15:15.290 --> 15:21.420
"Discriminatory comments about elves
occur regularly within Clover,

15:21.420 --> 15:25.050
and Thunder Pike had orders
to follow their example."

15:25.370 --> 15:27.410
"All damage incurred up to this point

15:27.410 --> 15:32.900
resulted from the lies and sedition of
Clover and, in particular, Yuke Feldio.

15:32.900 --> 15:35.310
Thunder Pike bears no responsibility."

15:35.310 --> 15:39.420
"Yuke Feldio feels genuine
remorse for what he has done

15:39.420 --> 15:41.700
and will apologize to Thunder Pike."

15:41.700 --> 15:48.410
"Thunder Pike will absorb Clover to
facilitate their rectification of the matter."

15:48.410 --> 15:49.450
What is all this?!

15:49.450 --> 15:51.970
It's about to be the truth.

15:51.970 --> 15:56.210
And then you're all going
to livestream an apology.

15:56.710 --> 16:00.120
I thought you were just a doofus
who happened to be a bit naïve,

16:00.120 --> 16:02.130
but now you're an actual sleaze—

16:04.280 --> 16:06.010
Not gonna sign it?

16:06.010 --> 16:12.520
How about I order this little girl
you love so much to serve Barry?

16:12.520 --> 16:15.330
If I sign it, you'd better let them go!

16:15.330 --> 16:18.520
Hey, now. You don't get to give me orders!

16:18.870 --> 16:22.440
Wasn't I always telling
you to know your place?

16:22.440 --> 16:25.800
Even after all the trouble we've
been through since you quit on us,

16:25.800 --> 16:28.410
you're out there enjoying every damn day!

16:28.410 --> 16:31.040
You piece of shit! Scum! Garbage!

16:31.040 --> 16:35.000
So I'm taking it all back—with interest!

16:35.000 --> 16:37.540
You've only been so
successful because of us!

16:37.540 --> 16:40.170
So you don't get to monopolize everything!

16:41.120 --> 16:43.430
Whoa, there, Simon. Don't kill him.

16:43.430 --> 16:45.930
This will all be for naught if he dies.

16:46.980 --> 16:48.470
I'm holding back.

16:48.470 --> 16:51.930
Oh, I know! Let's make an
example of that savage.

16:52.220 --> 16:57.440
Yuke, I'm going to order the girl with
the collar to kill the dark elf.

16:57.440 --> 17:00.920
Then you'll see how serious I am.

17:00.920 --> 17:01.780
Stop!

17:01.780 --> 17:03.390
Hold up, Simon.

17:03.390 --> 17:06.530
If you're gonna kill her, let me
have some fun with her first.

17:06.530 --> 17:08.240
Oh, that sounds fun, too.

17:08.240 --> 17:09.530
Wait!

17:09.530 --> 17:12.040
Just hang on! I'll sign it!

17:13.780 --> 17:15.440
Better do it quick.

17:15.440 --> 17:19.040
I really don't want to do
anything mean to a friend.

17:22.440 --> 17:24.420
Hurry it up!

17:29.800 --> 17:31.210
I have to sign it.

17:33.580 --> 17:34.500
An earthquake?!

17:34.500 --> 17:36.010
It's a big one!

17:37.840 --> 17:39.410
I think it's over.

17:39.410 --> 17:41.480
Okay, hurry up and sign it.

17:41.480 --> 17:42.940
Yuke!

17:43.270 --> 17:44.690
You don't feel that, Simon?

17:44.690 --> 17:45.690
Feel what?

17:45.690 --> 17:47.080
I don't know how to put it...

17:47.080 --> 17:49.700
It feels like the dungeon
is losing its stability.

17:49.700 --> 17:51.180
Enough of your—

17:53.700 --> 17:55.700
H-Hey, this looks bad!

17:57.290 --> 17:58.710
Barry! Camilla!

18:00.740 --> 18:01.710
Rain, wake up!

18:03.320 --> 18:04.420
We gotta get out!

18:04.420 --> 18:07.030
Shit! They took my Magic Bag!

18:07.030 --> 18:08.970
Of all the times for them
to be perceptive!

18:12.720 --> 18:14.720
Fall Control!

18:15.720 --> 18:16.790
(Fall Control)

18:16.790 --> 18:17.730
(Fall Control)
This is...

18:18.140 --> 18:19.880
Fall Control?

18:25.460 --> 18:26.650
Jamie?

18:28.580 --> 18:31.000
They're all okay, too. What a relief.

18:31.000 --> 18:31.990
Thanks, Jamie.

18:32.990 --> 18:34.240
It's okay...

18:38.650 --> 18:41.500
Jamie, you bitch! What the hell are you...

18:44.500 --> 18:45.500
Orcs!

18:46.520 --> 18:47.380
Jamie!

18:47.790 --> 18:48.870
I have to get this to Yuke!

18:48.870 --> 18:49.260
Hey!

18:49.770 --> 18:51.300
This is your gear!

18:55.380 --> 18:58.380
Check! Scroll of Sanctuary!

19:01.300 --> 19:03.480
Demon of sleep, begone.

19:03.480 --> 19:04.770
Awaken!

19:06.150 --> 19:09.030
I'm sorry.
I'll set you all free right away.

19:09.320 --> 19:11.660
Okay! The Scroll of Exit!

19:11.660 --> 19:13.160
Sanctuary!

19:13.720 --> 19:15.080
I'll help, too!

19:15.080 --> 19:16.910
Rain! And the rest of you!

19:17.480 --> 19:19.140
Gather close to me!

19:19.960 --> 19:21.920
Check! Scroll of Exit!

19:24.290 --> 19:26.800
Jamie! Get Simon
and the others out of here!

19:27.160 --> 19:30.550
A-Are you sure? After the
horrible things we did?

19:32.130 --> 19:34.300
The law ought to decide
what to do with them.

19:34.600 --> 19:36.170
They can't die here.

19:37.570 --> 19:38.840
Don't move!

19:43.940 --> 19:45.310
Yuke!

19:46.700 --> 19:47.780
Dryads!

19:48.850 --> 19:50.690
I'll slow them down! Go now!

19:51.990 --> 19:54.190
Simon, what are you thinking?!

19:55.470 --> 19:58.200
You're a real pro at seducing women, Yuke!

19:59.510 --> 20:03.460
This is bad! I can't use magic or do
anything while activating this scroll!

20:03.460 --> 20:06.050
Come on, you'd better save me right now!

20:06.050 --> 20:08.050
Otherwise this girl—

20:09.240 --> 20:10.210
Run, Rain!

20:10.210 --> 20:11.170
R-Right!

20:11.170 --> 20:12.090
Jamie!

20:12.090 --> 20:14.340
Come back! We're about to get out of here!

20:15.810 --> 20:16.650
Jamie!

20:19.870 --> 20:21.420
We can get out!

20:21.420 --> 20:22.430
Simon!

20:24.200 --> 20:26.000
Wait! Help us!

20:26.000 --> 20:28.230
We can't move! Please!

20:28.230 --> 20:32.610
Shut up! Get out on your own! I've had it!

20:33.860 --> 20:35.690
I'm getting out of here alive!

20:36.420 --> 20:37.870
Energy Bolt!

20:41.350 --> 20:43.870
I won't let you hurt Yuke
and his friends any more.

20:43.870 --> 20:45.960
You little bitch!

20:45.960 --> 20:49.130
Jamie, enough! Come back!
It's about to activate!

20:49.130 --> 20:51.250
Simon Berkley orders you!

20:51.250 --> 20:53.510
Sorry. Goodbye.

20:53.510 --> 20:54.470
Jamie!

20:54.470 --> 20:57.590
Wearer Rain! You are to save me—

20:59.220 --> 21:01.140
Huh? What?

21:01.640 --> 21:02.460
What?!

21:08.480 --> 21:09.390
- Stop!
- Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

21:09.390 --> 21:10.730
- I don't want to die! No!
- Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

21:11.740 --> 21:12.990
If it's come to this...

22:56.040 --> 22:56.920
(One Who Was Once a Friend)

22:56.920 --> 22:59.590
(One Who Was Once a Friend)
Next time, "One Who Was Once a Friend."

22:59.590 --> 23:01.010
(One Who Was Once a Friend)
